{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on the teardown repair (da1ba9e4): the isolated test-file exception applies; no further full gate for this repair\n\nDecision. Gate F at 9d775412 reached every stage and failed only in join-version.scope.test.ts, on a teardown error after its assertions passed. The repair at R 80a742bd changes only that test file, keeps its two cases, assertions and deadlines, touches no production code, configuration, dependency or shared helper, and the file is imported nowhere else. That is exactly the case docs/testing.md \"Follow-up after a gate\" describes, and the exception governs. The checker assesses gate F as the failed run together with the isolated follow-up: the changed compiler context and the whole owning test file, both 0/0 with closed streams, receipts 88fcc43d and 74d0d569. No stage was unreached, so nothing else runs.\n\nOn condition 1 of 1d0ffcab. It restated 31962e1f for a head whose repair regenerated a production module. Read it as: a later commit runs the gate again unless that commit changes only documents, or only a single failing test file under the docs/testing.md exception. The maintained rule in docs/testing.md governs; a ruling on one repair does not narrow it for the next. The asset regeneration was outside the exception because assets.ts is production; this teardown repair is inside it because nothing but the test changed.\n\nConditions.\n1. The evidence table keeps the failed gate at 40230449, the seal follow-up, the failed continuation at e9da1ba8, the failed gate F at 9d775412, and the R follow-up rows as separate rows with exit codes and digests. None becomes a pass; the checker's landing check reads them as the record.\n2. The note says in two sentences what in the test leaked the RPC resolve past teardown and why production has no equivalent (the test's own lifetime capture, not the Membership or Inbox code). If the cause is in production code, the exception does not apply and this ruling is void; say which.\n3. The head under review is R or a later documents-only commit. Any commit that changes source other than this test file runs the full gate again.\nRetire this question when read.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:da1ba9e4dfc2ea012511e39a9c3ec5e3be8d2af2 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fc6147591a9af6d61e588104e45348d320a63b80","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}